ise that  Lalo is already in Albuquerque we watch  his plan develop at his cool and  deliberate pace and we pick up with  Jimmy and Kim who are in a frantic race  against the clock these stories might be  happening in the same city but they  couldn't feel further apart and  everything on Kim and Jimmy's side  hinges on a character who couldn't be  further removed from the world that Lalo  and Gus inhabit different characters  different factions and different plans  but everyone does have one thing in  common they all think they know what's  going on and that they can control the  situation this is highlighted  beautifully in an early scene where  Howard startles a new hire who is there  to stock the refrigerator while we're  all thinking hey buddy don't put those  cans you just shook up in with the  others Howard calmly shows him how to  solve his problem what's more he learned  the technique when from the m in hhm  Charles McGill the fresh lawyer has no  idea who Chuck is a year and a half  after his death at least not from seeing  his image and that makes you think about  the legacy of the man who built the firm  into what it is which plays as some  uneasy foreshadowing of what's to come  for Howard Chuck knew Jimmy so well he  couldn't imagine anything going wrong  right up until the second it did Hamlin  doesn't believe he could make the same  mistake but ultimately he will as far as  D-Day is concerned the deck is stacked  against Howard in a way he wouldn't have  been able to anticipate the private  investigator he hired was indeed a plant  from Kim and Jimmy the whole time this  was something that started to become  apparent in the last episode but there  was the issue of not being able to  figure out how they would have got him  to hire the exact Pi they needed him to  it turns out they knew which agency hhm  uses for matters like this and so they  called them a receptionist telling her  they needed to update their contact  information the new number went straight  to a burner phone held by the pi Jimmy  and Kim hired and when Howard reached  out he dealt with him directly this  means he never had a chance into their  credit Jimmy and Kim's plan works  perfectly  first they have to reshoot the pictures  which is so much fun and so kinetic that  you almost forget about that Lalo teaser  Jimmy goes to convince Lenny to walk off  his shift and get some clutch  performances from the UNM film students  to recreate the bribe photographs with  the fake judge wearing a fake cast the  photo shoot starts out with this great  long sequence that plays like a Warner  where things wind up Tighter and Tighter  until it ends on a shot of Kim wrapping  the foe cast there's a couple of small  details here that lighten things up the  makeup girl is coming from rehearsal for  a live-action musical Tribute to The  Dark Crystal and if you're wondering why  the sound guy brings his boom mic to  photo shoots while someone has to make  it look like the shots were taken from  behind some cover it's notable that when  Kim shows up she refuses to head back to  Santa Fe for her meeting when Jimmy  suggests it helping those pro bono  clients is a distant memory in the midst  of the unfolding plan and later Howard  will finally lay out what's really  behind all of this sure they will get  money and it will be enough for her to  start her practice but they're really  doing this for fun this has never been  as clear as it is when they listen in on  the meeting the satisfaction of hearing  Howard's demise literally turns them on  to where they're grinding on the couch  before it's over and as mentioned it  does go off superbly the topical  solution on the pictures gets into  Howard's bloodstream as he thinks he's  being shown evidence of a bribe he  doesn't know who's in the pictures until  the judge walks into the meeting he  makes his accusation thinking he can  back it up only to have different  pictures of Jimmy handing the sound guy  who's wearing the handlebar mustache his  frisbee it's laugh out loud funny while  being devastating at the exact same time  it doesn't matter that he puts it all  together if if Cliff believes him or not  or whether Rich Schweikert is  disappointed about how it happened his  firm has to move to pressure to settle  and Cliff has to threaten Howard to  agree because there just isn't another  option I really liked how they ended  this for all the fun there was in the  lead up and how perfectly they paid off  all the setup the judge's reaction  enrich's conversation with Cliff paint a  great picture of how it looks from our  perspective there's no sense of Victory  no hooting no hollering there's no  dramatic moment with Howard nose diving  off the roof or anything like that it's  just an absolutely uncomfortable display  from The Golden Boy and we've already  peaked behind the curtains to know who  was responsible no matter how you feel  about Howard's character you can't help  but feel sad for him in that moment it  only gets worse from there Lalo has been  spending his time watching the laundry  company where Gus is building the super  lab he found out where that was from  Casper her and he makes a recording for  Donald audio revealing that he's still  alive and letting him know what Gus is  up to his plan is to kill the guards and  go inside to get that proof he's been  after but when he calls Hector he  realizes that he just gave himself away  when he hears that the phone line is  being monitored this is the rare  occasion where we see him lose his cool  but he recovers quickly after smashing  his folding chair he calls back into  Hector's dismay tells him he couldn't  find proof but will move against Gus  that night anyway this is misdirection  and he's able to see the security detail  react in real time it's not clear if he  anticipated that they were watching  Jimmy's apartment and wanted to draw  people away from there but that's what  ends up happening when Mike goes to warn  Gus he mentions that they pulled  everyone off of the low priority targets  their plan is to use Gus's two house  setup to their advantage put him in the  couple's house next door use the decoy  to make it look like he's in his house  alone and then take Lalo out when he  makes his move we'll have to wait and  see how that all plays out if it even  comes to that because he's got another  stop to make after seeing that cockroach  Kim and Jimmy are watching Classic  Movies waiting for Howard to show up  when the knock at the door happened I  half expected it to be Lolo which  provided an unexpected sense of relief  when it turned out to be Howard as Jimmy  opens the door you can't help but notice  that Kim reacts to the flicker of the  candle that's sitting on the table  Howard comes in and there's a little bit  of Kim and Jimmy acting like they don't  know what he's talking about which he  quickly points out that of course they  have to play it that way and then the  scene transcends whatever you thought it  might have been when Howard poses the  question everyone who watches the show  has been asking what did he do to  deserve this he then very succinctly  runs through all the reasons that we  know about which made me chuckle on a  personal level since they were all the  things I listed in my video a few weeks  ago it still doesn't quite make sense  and as Patrick Fabian who's always been  fantastic in the role takes things up to  another level that we've never seen he  puts it out there that they do it for  fun that they get off on it he reveals  what he really thinks about both of them  he agrees with Chuck that Jimmy can't  help himself he was born broken and will  never be different he says that he  thinks Kim is one of the smartest and  most promising human beings he's ever  known so he can't believe the choices  she's made there's a point here where he  tells her that she has a piece missing  and it feels like one of those  situations where someone tells you  something that you know to be true but  aren't willing to look at it's a telling  exchange that complicates things more  than it clears them up we know that he  has changed to become a better person  over the past few seasons but he's being  honest in the way that he looks at  people because he doesn't have anything  else to lose it's the part where Howard  gets to be right while still displaying  all the ugly parts of his character he  is all the things they think he is but  there is more to him in this episode  we've seen the good alongside the bad  and Jimmy and Kim are all the things  Howard thinks they are although the  sociopath allegation is a little  dramatic but there's more to them as  well and they did plan things out in a  way that could have worked there's a  moment where they've clearly won and  it's still true that he'll be able to  bounce back that he'll land on his feet  and he acknowledges this and we see some  of their Humanity when they react to the  news that his marriage is falling apart  it's not that they didn't plan things  out or even ignore the potential for  consequences it comes down to them not  having as much control over things as  they thought they did the same thing  they planned out to happen to Howard  happens to them and no amount of  planning could have accounted for the  situation they find themselves in when  the candle flickers again right before  that happens Howard vows to dedicate his  life to making sure everyone knows the  truth and I suppose that's a vow he's  able to keep Lalo enters the room and  Ray C horn and Bob Odenkirk match  Patrick fabian's incredible performance  when they realize what's happening the  look of Terror is so authentic and you  have to imagine for Jimmy this is like  seeing a ghost they try to get Howard to  leave but he's just getting started and  Tony Dalton sells the idea that he has  nothing to worry about even while he's  putting the silencer on his gun what  follows is a death that is absolutely  shocking even though you knew it was  going to happen it takes the idea of  Howard doesn't deserve this to a brand  new place his brains are splattered on  the painting that they use to plan out  his downfall and after he hits the  ground Lalo quiets them down and says  let's talk what happens next is  something we'll all be thinking about  until July 11th when episode 8 airs  there will be consequences it's hard to  say what those will be and it's hard to  know what Lolo has in mind for these two  that brought him over here in the first  place to me it seemed like Lalu might  have been surprised when he saw Mike  come out of the laundry and how quick  the response was maybe just how many  people were around in general it's  possible that his mistake tipped him off  that things were more dangerous than he  was expecting I also don't know how  they'll explain him never sending the  videotape to Eladio but maybe it will be  about him changing up his plans maybe  this is all related I don't know how  Jimmy and Kim fit into his plans but it  can't be good for either of them we know  what the consequences are for Howard  he's dead what's worse is that he'll  disappear with his legacy wiped away  thanks to this drug addiction narrative  that Jimmy and Kim So carefully crafted  he was the last of hhm standing so you  have to imagine that that will cease to  exist the final sequence is similar to  Drew Sharp's murder and Breaking Bad the  crazy plan works out but someone finds  themselves in the wrong place at the  wrong time I'd say it has the same  impact I'll also say again that it  doesn't matter if you like the character  or even if you were happy to see him  knocked down earlier in the episode no  one deserves what happens to him here  and Jimmy and Kim will be connected to  this since they saw it happen and won't  be able to say anything about it so just  a great episode it does all the things  that you expect Better Call Saul to do  well it looked great the performances  were stellar and it found a balance  between the funny and the dramatic there  were so many little things in this  episode that stand out that are in some  ways overshadowed by this crazy ending  what's more promising is the way they  brought things together plan an  execution addressed so many things we'd  been thinking about in the last three  episodes and delivered a confident  payoff it's also able to deliver what  you think think might happen with a  little bit of misdirection like Howard  not drinking caffeine to keep it from  being completely obvious plus it manages  to make the outcome that makes the most  sense still feel exciting which I guess  is really important when you're making a  prequel it was all really satisfying  little things like the pi being in on it  which was on the board to see if you go  back and look and big things like how  will this plan go wrong and what will  the unintended consequences be at the  beginning of the Season we had four  characters whose endings we weren't sure  about so far nacho and Howard's stories  both came to memorable ends and we still  have two to go I feel like my confidence  for how those will end is at an all-time  high regardless of which direction they  decide to go in there's so much more to  talk about but I think this is a good  place to leave things for this video  we'll be talking more about this episode  on Tuesday night in the live stream at  9pm Eastern and I'll have a couple of  other videos videos out later this week  for now let me know in the comments what  you thought about this episode if you  thought the payoff was worth the setup  and what you think will happen next  please like this video If you enjoyed it  please subscribe to my channel if you  haven't already and thanks for watching  I'll talk to you soon

